---
title: Cantonese Soy Sauce Chicken (Si You Gai 四友雞)
description: Traditional Cantonese soy sauce chicken braise with a sweet-salty glaze and aromatic spices. Incredibly tender meat that's marinated in the hot liquid.
prep time: 10 minutes
cook time: 45 minutes
servings: 4
tags:
  - chicken
  - cantonese
  - braised
  - chinese
source: https://thewoksoflife.com/cantonese-soy-sauce-chicken
cuisine: Chinese
course: Main
---

== Prepare the Braising Liquid ==
In a #large pot{}, combine @light soy sauce{240%g}, @dark soy sauce{120%g}, @sugar{100%g}, @Shaoxing wine{60%g}, @water{750%g}, @ginger{4%thick slices}, @scallions{4%pieces, 5 cm}, @star anise{3%whole}, and @cinnamon stick{1%small}. Bring to a boil over medium-high heat.

== Braise the Chicken ==
-- Ensure the skin faces up so it doesn't tear on the bottom of the pot
Carefully lower the @bone-in, skin-on chicken thighs{1.2%kg} into the liquid (skin side up).
Reduce the heat to a gentle simmer, cover with a #lid{}, and cook for ~{30%minutes}.

== Rest and Serve ==
-- Resting in the hot liquid makes the chicken incredibly tender and flavorful
Turn off the heat. Let the chicken sit in the hot liquid with the lid on for ~{15%minutes} to absorb the color and flavor.
Remove, chop into serving pieces, and drizzle with a spoonful of the braising liquid.
